tions/create">Shopify automation templates</a> and <a href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/35510464880027">Klaviyo cart versus checkout entry</a>. Compare matched subscription, usage and integration quotes for the same eligible audience.</p> : <p>Primary references checked November 25, 2026: <a href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/promoting-marketing/create-marketing/shopify-messaging/marketing-automations/create">Shopify automation documentation</a> and <a href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115002774932">Klaviyo flow documentation</a>. Compare subscription, usage and integration quotes for the same eligible audience.</p>}
        <h2>Acceptance decision record</h2>
        <p>{editorial.acceptance}</p>
        <p>Record candidate, account configuration, fixture inputs, expected versus actual disposition, owner and decision date. A pass here means the proposed exercise passed in that configuration; it is not a supplier-wide certification or an observed result reported by this guide.</p>
        <h2>Shared baseline controls</h2>
        {isStock ? <><p>Keep email stock-notice permission per subscription and variant, separate from newsletter, SMS and service purposes. Maintain one sender and a stable store/customer/subscription/variant/restock-episode key. Capture source, observation timestamp and a merchant-approved freshness limit for sellable availability; physical quantity alone is insufficient. Refresh permission, matching purchases, publication, destination, availability and approved copy before each dispatch. Hold unknown state. No email reserves inventory.</p><p>Use a finite contact budget and episode expiry. Withdrawal, matching purchase or expiry closes pending work without automatic reopening on later inventory updates. Reconcile ambiguous acknowledgements before retry; a skipped filter does not prove all later jobs stopped. Rollback pauses dispatch and records every pending job as held, cancelled or acknowledged before another sender takes ownership. Keep required service notices separately owned. Demonstrate these requirements in the offered account.</p></> : isLaunch ? <><p>Assign one sender and a stable store/release/customer/message key. Record stock and entitlement sources, refresh timestamps and the release timezone. Before each dispatch, check current permission, relevant purchase, publication, allocation, copy approval and cutoff. Hold unknown state. Email selection does not reserve inventory or grant access.</p><p>Use a finite contact budget and explicit expiry. Reconcile uncertain acknowledgements before replay; a skipped action does not prove later jobs are cancelled. On rollback pause dispatch, inventory pending jobs and record held, cancelled or acknowledged disposition before transferring ownership. Keep receipts and required service notices separately owned. All controls here are proposed demonstrations, not automatic capability guarantees.</p></> : isWinBack ? <><p>Define inactivity from complete order history and a declared product, season or membership rule. Missing history is unknown state. Assign a stable customer/last-order/rule episode key and one sender. Before every action refresh purchase, permission, service holds, offer validity and final-contact disposition. A skipped action is not proof that all later actions are cancelled; Klaviyo documents repeated profile checks, so demonstrate permanent episode closure separately.</p><p>Specify a finite contact budget and a final preference or stop path. Completion, withdrawal or a return purchase closes that episode; a changed rule cannot silently restart it. Keep billing and required service notices separately owned. Reconcile uncertain acknowledgements before retry, expire stale offers and retain a disposition for every pending job. On rollback pause dispatch and inventory held, cancelled and acknowledged work before transferring senders. These are acceptance requirements, not automatic supplier guarantees.</p></> : isPost ? <><p>Payment starts this proposed relationship workflow; it does not prove shipment, receipt or product use. Maintain order and line-level fulfillment, refund and support state with timestamps. Recheck current permission and suppression at dispatch. A marketing withdrawal holds queued promotion; required receipts and service notices retain their own callers and permissions. Do not turn an order contact or gift recipient into a marketing subscriber.</p><p>Use a stable store/order/purpose key and one sender owner. A new purchase changes owned-product recommendations rather than ending all useful education. Cancellation, refund, delivery exception or an unresolved use-related case must route affected copy to review. Hold unknown state; reconcile ambiguous acknowledgements before retry. On rollback pause dispatch, inventory every pending job and record held, cancelled or acknowledged disposition before switching senders. Demonstrate these controls in the configured account; no automatic cancellation is assumed.</p></> : isCart ? <><p>Record purpose and email permission separately. Recheck permission, purchase, cart contents and suppression at dispatch. Anonymous browsing is not an identified recoverable cart. Link cart token, checkout ID and stable customer identity explicitly; a checkout transition must retire competing cart outreach. Assign one sender and queue owner per intent. Required receipts, payment and service notices keep their separate callers and permissions.</p><p>Choose delay from the actual objection, stock freshness and delivery promise. Start with useful checkout help; any discount needs approved eligibility, version, expiry and stacking rules. Hold unknown state, reconcile ambiguous acknowledgements and expire stale jobs. Before rollback, pause dispatch, inventory pending jobs and record whether each is cancelled, held or already acknowledged; do not drain the old queue into a new sender. Demonstrate these controls rather than assuming automatic cancellation.</p></> : <p>Record purpose and email permission separately. Recheck current permission, purchase and suppression state at dispatch. Use stable event and identity keys, cancel stale queued jobs and assign one sender per welcome purpose. Keep receipts and required service notices under their own ownership. Choose delays from the promise and operational constraints rather than a universal welcome cadence.</p>}
        <h2>Measurement and operator handover</h2>
        {isStock ? <p>Descriptive sent-population measure: {editorial.denominator}. Report raw counts and sparse-count uncertainty; zero sent units has no rate. For causal comparison randomize eligible request identities before dispatch, retain assignments after purchase, withdrawal, stock loss or expiry and compare matching buyers per assigned unit over the same declared window. Keep this separate from sent-only rates and vendor attribution. Where one customer has several requests, randomize by customer to avoid cross-arm contact and report clustering and unit definitions.</p> : isLaunch ? <p>Descriptive sent-population measure: {editorial.denominator}. Deduplicate the stated unit and report raw counts; zero recipients has no rate. This is not a causal lift estimate. If using a randomized holdout, assign before dispatch and retain every eligible assignment after expiry, purchase or suppression. Compare unique launch buyers per assigned identity over the same declared window, separately from sent-only rates; for food also report fulfilled orders per assigned identity. Report sparse-count uncertainty and vendor attribution separately.</p> : isWinBack ? <p>Denominator: {editorial.denominator}. Assign a randomized holdout before dispatch where feasible; retain assignment after purchase, withdrawal, expiry or final contact. Declare one observation window and compare unique returning paid buyers per assigned eligible buyer. The historical entry order is excluded; multiple return orders do not multiply the buyer count. Report sparse counts and uncertainty; zero eligible buyers has no rate. Keep vendor-attributed revenue descriptive.</p> : isPost ? <p>Denominator: {editorial.denominator}. Assign a randomized holdout before dispatch where feasible and retain original assignment after refund, withdrawal or expiry. Declare the observation window and compare repeat buyers per assigned eligible buyer, alongside education engagement, support contacts and refunds. Exclude the entry order from repeat-purchase counts, deduplicate buyers and report sparse-count uncertainty; zero eligible buyers has no rate. Vendor-attributed revenue is descriptive.</p> : <p>Denominator: {editorial.denominator}. Assign a randomized holdout before dispatch where feasible; retain assignment when a job later expires or a customer purchases. Compare paid orders per assigned eligible identity over the same declared observation window; report uncertainty when counts are sparse. Vendor-attributed revenue is a separate descriptive measure.</p>}
