        <h2>Fixed-goods economics</h2>
        <p>Compare contribution after product cost, discounts, refunds, payment fees and variable fulfillment with the same costs in the holdout. Deduct incremental platform, integration and operator costs once for the same period. Keep migration and overlap costs separate from recurring costs. A paid order is not all profit; no assumed recovered-order count establishes that an app pays for itself.</p>
        <h2>FAQ</h2>
        <h3>When should another app enter the shortlist?</h3>
        <p>When the proposed account demonstration fails a required field, dispatch guard or purchase exit and another candidate can demonstrate that requirement with an owned integration. Keep a useful existing sender when it passes.</p>
        {isStock ? <><h3>Does a restock notice reserve the requested item?</h3><p>No. Availability is an observation with a source and timestamp. Recheck the exact variant and destination before dispatch, avoid reservation language and close or hold stale jobs. Stock-notice permission does not enroll a requester into unrelated promotions.</p></> : isLaunch ? <><h3>Does audience selection guarantee that a launch promise is still valid?</h3><p>No. Refresh the relevant variant, access entitlement, approved copy and fulfillment window at dispatch. Hold unknown or expired state, reconcile the queue and demonstrate purchase exit. A segment alone neither reserves stock nor grants storefront access.</p></> : isWinBack ? <><h3>Should every inactive buyer receive another discount?</h3><p>No. Inactivity can reflect seasonality, a gift, a paused plan or a service problem. Start with the relevant preference or return job, preserve a no-incentive comparison and close the episode after its declared final contact. A click alone does not prove a return purchase or grant a new series.</p></> : isPost ? <><h3>Does payment mean the customer is ready for a cross-sell?</h3><p>No. Confirm the relevant product was received and that current ownership, service, refund and permission state permit the offer. Useful approved education can precede selling; keep required order notices separately owned.</p></> : isCart ? <><h3>Should every abandoned cart receive a discount?</h3><p>No. A cart can need size guidance, a delivery answer or payment help. Preserve approved offer terms and compare contribution with the assigned holdout before expanding incentives.</p></> : <><h3>Must the welcome contain a discount?</h3>
